1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Twenty answers light up: the app's code.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Proven bricks fly in by shelf and snap into kits.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The tables build themselves, column by column.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The build prompts write themselves.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Every test ticks green.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The app goes live on the dashboard. Vision 2029, illustrative.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
This is the App Factory. It turns one idea into a live, safe app.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Every app has the same four parts: screens you see, tables that hold data, rules, and people.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Most apps are hand-made from nothing. Each one has its own gaps.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
A factory uses one road for every idea: nine stages, from Idea to Operate.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The stages happen in rooms, like Reception, Research, Rig, Reactor, Runway and Radar.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Between stages sit gates. Work moves on only when its checks pass.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
At six gates a person says yes or no. The rest open by themselves.

14
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Apps are built from proven parts called bricks, sorted on eight shelves and grouped into kits.

15
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Walls keep each business and each customer apart. They are tested again and again.

16
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Same road, same checks, same parts. That is what makes a factory app safe.
